WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.157
Easy Science. Why Do We Need Sleep?

00:00:03.157 --> 00:00:06.290
We spend about one third of our lives asleep.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.129
That seems like a lot of time doing nothing.

00:00:09.129 --> 00:00:13.363
But while we sleep, the body and the brain are very busy.

00:00:13.363 --> 00:00:16.197
During sleep the body repairs itself.

00:00:16.197 --> 00:00:17.988
Muscles rest and grow.

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:20.781
Children grow most while they are asleep.

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:25.326
The body also fights sickness better when it has had enough sleep.

00:00:25.326 --> 00:00:28.166
The brain does important work at night too.

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:32.375
During the day we see, hear and learn many new things.

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:34.682
At night the brain goes through them.

00:00:34.682 --> 00:00:38.870
It keeps what is important and puts it into our long memory.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.339
That is why a good night's sleep after studying helps us remember.

00:00:43.339 --> 00:00:46.524
The brain also cleans itself while we sleep.

00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:49.795
It washes away waste that builds up during the day.

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:52.406
What happens if we do not sleep enough?

00:00:52.406 --> 00:00:54.838
We feel tired, of course.

00:00:54.838 --> 00:01:00.609
But we also think more slowly, forget things, and get angry more easily.

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:04.538
Most adults need seven to nine hours of sleep each night.

00:01:04.538 --> 00:01:07.037
Children and teenagers need more.

00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:10.961
Scientists still do not understand everything about sleep.

00:01:10.961 --> 00:01:15.664
But they all agree on one thing: we cannot live well without it.
